Transactions and ACID Properties Lab

Description

This project uses PostgreSQL to practice database transactions and understand the ACID properties.

Database Structure

The database contains seven tables: customers, accounts, products, inventory, orders, order_items, and audit_log.

Topics Covered

Transactions – managing multiple SQL operations as one logical unit.

BEGIN, COMMIT, ROLLBACK – starting, saving, and undoing transactions.

ACID Properties – Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, and Durability.

Isolation Levels – READ UNCOMMITTED, READ COMMITTED, REPEATABLE READ, and SERIALIZABLE.

Savepoints – creating intermediate points and rolling back selected operations.

Transaction Management – handling errors, maintaining data consistency, and working with concurrent transactions.

Conclusion

This lab provides practical experience with PostgreSQL transactions and demonstrates how ACID properties help maintain database reliability and data integrity.
